{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have a working "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call and you want it to remember context across turns or\nsessions. By the end of this guide, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" recalls relevant memory into the\nprompt and saves each finished turn through a real adapter, scoped safely from your\nserver-validated session."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Want the full contract first? See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"step-1-install-the-package","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 1: Install the package"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-memory\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-memory\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-memory\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-memory\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-memory\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-memory\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-memory\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-memory\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-memory"},{"type":"text","value":" ships "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":", the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MemoryAdapter"},{"type":"text","value":" contract, and the\nbuilt-in and vendor adapters (each on its own subpath)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"step-2-pick-an-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 2: Pick an adapter"}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In-memory:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inMemory()"},{"type":"text","value":" is zero-dependency and stores records in a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Map"},{"type":"text","value":". Use it\nfor local development, tests, and single-process demos. Records vanish on restart."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Redis:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis({ redis })"},{"type":"text","value":" persists across restarts and shares state across\nprocesses. Bring your own client ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ioredis"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redis"},{"type":"text","value":" via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fromNodeRedis"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vendors:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hindsight()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mem0()"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"honcho()"},{"type":"text","value":" delegate to a hosted memory service."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom adapters implement the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" contract. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./custom-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"step-3-wire-memorymiddleware-into-chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 3: Wire "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start with the in-memory adapter, the fastest path to a working setup:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\nconst memory = inMemory()\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello' }],\n  middleware: [\n    memoryMiddleware({\n      adapter: memory,\n      scope: { threadId: 'demo-thread', userId: 'alice' },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each turn, the middleware recalls relevant memory into the system prompt (lexical scoring\nby default), then deferred-saves the user and assistant turn after the stream finishes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you're ready to ship, swap the adapter and keep everything else the same:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import Redis from 'ioredis'\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport { redis } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/redis'\nimport type { MemoryScope } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\n\ndeclare const scope: MemoryScope // from Step 5\n\nconst client = new Redis(process.env.REDIS_URL ?? 'redis://localhost:6379')\nconst memory = redis({ redis: client })\n\nmemoryMiddleware({ adapter: memory, scope })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using a hosted service? Swap "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inMemory()"},{"type":"text","value":" for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hindsight({ user })"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mem0({ user })"},{"type":"text","value":",\nor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"honcho({ user })"},{"type":"text","value":". The middleware wiring is identical. The adapter maps\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" onto the vendor API."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"step-4-semantic-scoring-optional","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 4: Semantic scoring (optional)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The built-in adapters score lexically by default. Pass an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embedder"},{"type":"text","value":" for semantic recall\nwhen scopes grow large or queries don't share keywords with stored text:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import OpenAI from 'openai'\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\nconst openai = new OpenAI()\n\nconst memory = inMemory({\n  embedder: {\n    async embed(text) {\n      const result = await openai.embeddings.create({\n        model: 'text-embedding-3-small',\n        input: text,\n      })\n      const embedding = result.data[0]?.embedding\n      if (!embedding) throw new Error('embedding request returned no vector')\n      return embedding\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"step-5-derive-scope-server-side","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 5: Derive scope server-side"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scope"},{"type":"text","value":" is the isolation boundary. Static scopes are fine for fixtures, but in any real\napp derive scope per request from server-validated session data, never from the request\nbody."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport type { ModelMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport type { MemoryAdapter } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\n\n// From earlier steps / your auth layer.\ndeclare const messages: Array<ModelMessage>\ndeclare const memory: MemoryAdapter\ndeclare const session: { userId: string; threadId: string }\ndeclare function getSession(ctx: unknown): { threadId: string; userId: string }\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages,\n  context: { session }, // attached by your auth middleware, not from req.body\n  middleware: [\n    memoryMiddleware({\n      adapter: memory,\n      scope: (ctx) => {\n        const session = getSession(ctx)\n        return { threadId: session.threadId, userId: session.userId }\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the client, nothing changes for memory wiring — consume the same stream as any\nother "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" endpoint:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  })\n  // Memory is entirely server-side; the client only sees the usual message stream.\n  return (\n    // render messages, input, sendMessage, isLoading…\n    null\n  )\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-to-go-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where to go next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" contract, scope, and how a turn flows"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":": every adapter's options, with an example of each"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./operating","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Operating memory"}]},{"type":"text","value":": options, telemetry, devtools events, and failures"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./custom-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": implement "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recall"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"save"},{"type":"text","value":" for a backend that isn't shipped"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"step-1-install-the-package","text":"Step 1: Install the package","level":2},{"id":"step-2-pick-an-adapter","text":"Step 2: Pick an adapter","level":2},{"id":"step-3-wire-memorymiddleware-into-chat","text":"Step 3: Wire memoryMiddleware into chat()","level":2},{"id":"step-4-semantic-scoring-optional","text":"Step 4: Semantic scoring (optional)","level":2},{"id":"step-5-derive-scope-server-side","text":"Step 5: Derive scope server-side","level":2},{"id":"where-to-go-next","text":"Where to go next","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have a working `chat()` call and you want it to remember context across turns or\nsessions. By the end of this guide, `memoryMiddleware` recalls relevant memory into the\nprompt and saves each finished turn through a real adapter, scoped safely from your\nserver-validated session.\n\n> Want the full contract first? See the [Overview](./overview).\n\n## Step 1: Install the package\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-memory\nvue: @tanstack/ai-memory\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-memory\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-memory\npreact: @tanstack/ai-memory\nangular: @tanstack/ai-memory\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-memory\noctane: @tanstack/ai-memory\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n`@tanstack/ai-memory` ships `memoryMiddleware`, the `MemoryAdapter` contract, and the\nbuilt-in and vendor adapters (each on its own subpath).\n\n## Step 2: Pick an adapter\n\n> **In-memory:** `inMemory()` is zero-dependency and stores records in a `Map`. Use it\n> for local development, tests, and single-process demos. Records vanish on restart.\n>\n> **Redis:** `redis({ redis })` persists across restarts and shares state across\n> processes. Bring your own client (`ioredis`, or `redis` via `fromNodeRedis`).\n>\n> **Vendors:** `hindsight()`, `mem0()`, and `honcho()` delegate to a hosted memory service.\n\nCustom adapters implement the `recall`/`save` contract. See [Custom Adapter](./custom-adapter).\n\n## Step 3: Wire `memoryMiddleware` into `chat()`\n\nStart with the in-memory adapter, the fastest path to a working setup:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\nconst memory = inMemory()\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello' }],\n  middleware: [\n    memoryMiddleware({\n      adapter: memory,\n      scope: { threadId: 'demo-thread', userId: 'alice' },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nEach turn, the middleware recalls relevant memory into the system prompt (lexical scoring\nby default), then deferred-saves the user and assistant turn after the stream finishes.\n\nWhen you're ready to ship, swap the adapter and keep everything else the same:\n\n```ts\nimport Redis from 'ioredis'\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport { redis } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/redis'\nimport type { MemoryScope } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\n\ndeclare const scope: MemoryScope // from Step 5\n\nconst client = new Redis(process.env.REDIS_URL ?? 'redis://localhost:6379')\nconst memory = redis({ redis: client })\n\nmemoryMiddleware({ adapter: memory, scope })\n```\n\n> Using a hosted service? Swap `inMemory()` for `hindsight({ user })`, `mem0({ user })`,\n> or `honcho({ user })`. The middleware wiring is identical. The adapter maps\n> `recall`/`save` onto the vendor API.\n\n## Step 4: Semantic scoring (optional)\n\nThe built-in adapters score lexically by default. Pass an `embedder` for semantic recall\nwhen scopes grow large or queries don't share keywords with stored text:\n\n```ts\nimport OpenAI from 'openai'\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\nconst openai = new OpenAI()\n\nconst memory = inMemory({\n  embedder: {\n    async embed(text) {\n      const result = await openai.embeddings.create({\n        model: 'text-embedding-3-small',\n        input: text,\n      })\n      const embedding = result.data[0]?.embedding\n      if (!embedding) throw new Error('embedding request returned no vector')\n      return embedding\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Step 5: Derive scope server-side\n\n`scope` is the isolation boundary. Static scopes are fine for fixtures, but in any real\napp derive scope per request from server-validated session data, never from the request\nbody.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport type { ModelMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport type { MemoryAdapter } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\n\n// From earlier steps / your auth layer.\ndeclare const messages: Array<ModelMessage>\ndeclare const memory: MemoryAdapter\ndeclare const session: { userId: string; threadId: string }\ndeclare function getSession(ctx: unknown): { threadId: string; userId: string }\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages,\n  context: { session }, // attached by your auth middleware, not from req.body\n  middleware: [\n    memoryMiddleware({\n      adapter: memory,\n      scope: (ctx) => {\n        const session = getSession(ctx)\n        return { threadId: session.threadId, userId: session.userId }\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nOn the client, nothing changes for memory wiring — consume the same stream as any\nother `chat()` endpoint:\n\n```ts\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  })\n  // Memory is entirely server-side; the client only sees the usual message stream.\n  return (\n    // render messages, input, sendMessage, isLoading…\n    null\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Overview](./overview): the `recall`/`save` contract, scope, and how a turn flows\n- [Adapters](./adapters): every adapter's options, with an example of each\n- [Operating memory](./operating): options, telemetry, devtools events, and failures\n- [Custom Adapter](./custom-adapter): implement `recall`/`save` for a backend that isn't shipped\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Quickstart\nid: memory-quickstart\norder: 2\ndescription: \"Add cross-session memory to a TanStack AI chat() call: install the package, pick a recall/save adapter, wire memoryMiddleware, and derive scope server-side.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - memory\n  - quickstart\n  - in-memory adapter\n  - redis adapter\n  - chat middleware\n---\n\nYou have a working `chat()` call and you want it to remember context across turns or\nsessions. By the end of this guide, `memoryMiddleware` recalls relevant memory into the\nprompt and saves each finished turn through a real adapter, scoped safely from your\nserver-validated session.\n\n> Want the full contract first? See the [Overview](./overview).\n\n## Step 1: Install the package\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-memory\nvue: @tanstack/ai-memory\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-memory\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-memory\npreact: @tanstack/ai-memory\nangular: @tanstack/ai-memory\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-memory\noctane: @tanstack/ai-memory\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n`@tanstack/ai-memory` ships `memoryMiddleware`, the `MemoryAdapter` contract, and the\nbuilt-in and vendor adapters (each on its own subpath).\n\n## Step 2: Pick an adapter\n\n> **In-memory:** `inMemory()` is zero-dependency and stores records in a `Map`. Use it\n> for local development, tests, and single-process demos. Records vanish on restart.\n>\n> **Redis:** `redis({ redis })` persists across restarts and shares state across\n> processes. Bring your own client (`ioredis`, or `redis` via `fromNodeRedis`).\n>\n> **Vendors:** `hindsight()`, `mem0()`, and `honcho()` delegate to a hosted memory service.\n\nCustom adapters implement the `recall`/`save` contract. See [Custom Adapter](./custom-adapter).\n\n## Step 3: Wire `memoryMiddleware` into `chat()`\n\nStart with the in-memory adapter, the fastest path to a working setup:\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\nconst memory = inMemory()\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello' }],\n  middleware: [\n    memoryMiddleware({\n      adapter: memory,\n      scope: { threadId: 'demo-thread', userId: 'alice' },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nEach turn, the middleware recalls relevant memory into the system prompt (lexical scoring\nby default), then deferred-saves the user and assistant turn after the stream finishes.\n\nWhen you're ready to ship, swap the adapter and keep everything else the same:\n\n```ts\nimport Redis from 'ioredis'\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport { redis } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/redis'\nimport type { MemoryScope } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\n\ndeclare const scope: MemoryScope // from Step 5\n\nconst client = new Redis(process.env.REDIS_URL ?? 'redis://localhost:6379')\nconst memory = redis({ redis: client })\n\nmemoryMiddleware({ adapter: memory, scope })\n```\n\n> Using a hosted service? Swap `inMemory()` for `hindsight({ user })`, `mem0({ user })`,\n> or `honcho({ user })`. The middleware wiring is identical. The adapter maps\n> `recall`/`save` onto the vendor API.\n\n## Step 4: Semantic scoring (optional)\n\nThe built-in adapters score lexically by default. Pass an `embedder` for semantic recall\nwhen scopes grow large or queries don't share keywords with stored text:\n\n```ts\nimport OpenAI from 'openai'\nimport { inMemory } from '@tanstack/ai-memory/in-memory'\n\nconst openai = new OpenAI()\n\nconst memory = inMemory({\n  embedder: {\n    async embed(text) {\n      const result = await openai.embeddings.create({\n        model: 'text-embedding-3-small',\n        input: text,\n      })\n      const embedding = result.data[0]?.embedding\n      if (!embedding) throw new Error('embedding request returned no vector')\n      return embedding\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Step 5: Derive scope server-side\n\n`scope` is the isolation boundary. Static scopes are fine for fixtures, but in any real\napp derive scope per request from server-validated session data, never from the request\nbody.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { memoryMiddleware } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\nimport type { ModelMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport type { MemoryAdapter } from '@tanstack/ai-memory'\n\n// From earlier steps / your auth layer.\ndeclare const messages: Array<ModelMessage>\ndeclare const memory: MemoryAdapter\ndeclare const session: { userId: string; threadId: string }\ndeclare function getSession(ctx: unknown): { threadId: string; userId: string }\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  messages,\n  context: { session }, // attached by your auth middleware, not from req.body\n  middleware: [\n    memoryMiddleware({\n      adapter: memory,\n      scope: (ctx) => {\n        const session = getSession(ctx)\n        return { threadId: session.threadId, userId: session.userId }\n      },\n    }),\n  ],\n})\n```\n\nOn the client, nothing changes for memory wiring — consume the same stream as any\nother `chat()` endpoint:\n\n```ts\nimport { useChat, fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  })\n  // Memory is entirely server-side; the client only sees the usual message stream.\n  return (\n    // render messages, input, sendMessage, isLoading…\n    null\n  )\n}\n```\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Overview](./overview): the `recall`/`save` contract, scope, and how a turn flows\n- [Adapters](./adapters): every adapter's options, with an example of each\n- [Operating memory](./operating): options, telemetry, devtools events, and failures\n- [Custom Adapter](./custom-adapter): implement `recall`/`save` for a backend that isn't shipped\n"}
